{"type":"message","id":"e0c3ed0d","parentId":"a02851bb","timestamp":"2026-05-29T22:16:27.596Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `/api/send` endpoint returns the same greeting. That's not the send endpoint. Let me try other paths - maybe the send endpoint is at the root path but needs to be a GET, or maybe it's a different route entirely.\n\nLooking at the previous attempts:\n- `POST /send` = error 1101 (Cloudflare error - route not found)\n- `POST /api/send` = \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" (returns same as root)\n- `POST /message` = \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" \n- `POST /messages` = returns a message history (when it contains content)\n\n\n- `POST /` = \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\"\n\nIt seems like POST requests without a recognized route are falling back to the root handler, which returns the greeting. So `/send` should work as a POST endpoint, but it's returning 1101 instead of reaching the handler. Maybe the API key is invalid for this endpoint, or there's a different issue with the route configuration. Let me try a few more endpoints to debug this - `/msg`, `/new`, `/write`, and a couple others.","thinkingSignature":"834a29f77e04381c194c0eb517182d3e2049ea109782773071206bf7f029bf3a"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_1ttxs8tgijp8_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/api/v1/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"test\"}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":55,"output":334,"cacheRead":77184,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":77573,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780092980133,"responseId":"06694334736913fd4c327897d3b4b47d"}}
