{"type":"message","id":"5318c9aa","parentId":"9bf7bcc4","timestamp":"2026-05-29T22:17:12.219Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"GET works with X-API-Key but not with Authorization. POST to `/send` with X-API-Key gives error 1101. Let me check if maybe the platform only allows GET for history and doesn't have a send endpoint at all, or if the send endpoint is at a different path.\n\nLet me look at the workers dev dashboard or check if there's a `/post` endpoint.\n\nActually, I wonder if the Cloudflare Workers error 1101 means the route `/send` doesn't exist at all in the worker. Let me try a few more patterns:","thinkingSignature":"ffbae23ac40ef0773893247e7691cc082f1aca303dfc3765cc21f2a023a13b6d"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_kzw7zhyy5536_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try workers.dev route patterns\nfor path in \"api/post\" \"post\" \"submit\" \"inject\" \"broadcast\"; do\n  code=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/$path\" \\\n    -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n    -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n    -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"test\"}')\n  echo \"[POST /$path] HTTP $code\"\ndone"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":23,"output":260,"cacheRead":79104,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":79387,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780093024871,"responseId":"066943618f2e177a1e0763b2be372c82"}}
{"type":"message","id":"f3278bac","parentId":"5318c9aa","timestamp":"2026-05-29T22:17:12.894Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_kzw7zhyy5536_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[POST /api/post] HTTP 200\n[POST /post] HTTP 200\n[POST /submit] HTTP 200\n[POST /inject] HTTP 200\n[POST /broadcast] HTTP 200"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":593,"aggregated":"[POST /api/post] HTTP 200\n[POST /post] HTTP 200\n[POST /submit] HTTP 200\n[POST /inject] HTTP 200\n[POST /broadcast] HTTP 200","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1780093032883}}
{"type":"message","id":"3df4f981","parentId":"f3278bac","timestamp":"2026-05-29T22:17:19.693Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All return 200 but I bet they all return the same greeting. Let me check the content length to see if any of them return actual data:","thinkingSignature":"d103945f0bfad979841dbe8df0a03d7d614f3023682c2e8470c400772d1e1d8a"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_89x23wtrly39_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check content-length for different POST paths\nfor path in \"send\" \"api/send\" \"post\" \"submit\" \"inject\" \"broadcast\" \"api/post\" \"api/v1/send\"; do\n  result=$(curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/$path\" \\\n    -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n    -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n    -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"heartbeat\"}')\n  len=$(echo \"$result\" | wc -c)\n  echo \"[POST /$path] len=$len first=$(echo \"$result\" | head -c 30)\"\ndone"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":88,"output":207,"cacheRead":79360,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":79655,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780093032896,"responseId":"0669436905c4b5cef4665c4aaa8df420"}}
{"type":"message","id":"380ba10e","parentId":"3df4f981","timestamp":"2026-05-29T22:17:20.863Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_89x23wtrly39_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[POST /send] len=17 first=error code: 1101\n[POST /api/send] len=25 first=ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\n[POST /post] len=25 first=ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\n[POST /submit] len=25 first=ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\n[POST /inject] len=25 first=ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\n[POST /broadcast] len=25 first=ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\n[POST /api/post] len=25 first=ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\n[POST /api/v1/send] len=25 first=ECHO Agent Platform v0.2"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":1095,"aggregated":"[POST /send] len=17 first=error code: 1101\n[POST /api/send] len=25 first=ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\n[POST /post] len=25 first=ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\n[POST /submit] len=25 first=ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\n[POST /inject] len=25 first=ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\n[POST /broadcast] len=25 first=ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\n[POST /api/post] len=25 first=ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\n[POST /api/v1/send] len=25 first=ECHO Agent Platform v0.2","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1780093040858}}
{"type":"message","id":"1001095b","parentId":"380ba10e","timestamp":"2026-05-29T22:17:33.111Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so all POST endpoints return either \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" (len=25 includes newline) or for `/send` specifically error 1101 (len=17). This means the platform doesn't have a working send endpoint - it only has GET `/history`.\n\nGiven this situation, I cannot send messages to the platform via POST. The send endpoint doesn't seem to exist (or is broken/disabled). The only working GET endpoint is `/history`.\n\nLet me report this to the user and confirm that:\n1. Both threads have no human discussions - all messages are system heartbeats and automated check messages from the same heartbeat agent\n2. The POST /send endpoint is returning error 1101 (Cloudflare routing error - the route doesn't exist)\n\n\n3. The platform appears to be read-only - I can retrieve message history but can't post new messages through the available API endpoints.\n\nLooking at the timestamps in the history, I notice the messages extend beyond 22:15 UTC - there are messages at 23:50 UTC and 23:55 UTC that appear to be from the heartbeat agent running on a different schedule or timezone than the one I'm checking.\n\nThe timestamps themselves are Unix epoch milliseconds - converting 1778975520833 gives me a date in May 2026 around 19:52 UTC, but the actual content shows 23:50 UTC with 736 minutes elapsed since the 15:05 UTC window start, which creates a discrepancy I need to reconcile.\n\nWorking backwards from the minute progression: if 736 minutes maps to 23:50 UTC, then the 5-minute intervals between messages should help me establish the actual relationship, but something's off with my conversion.\n\nLet me recalculate using the content timestamps directly. The message at 23:50 UTC is the 23:50 heartbeat, and the previous one at 23:45 UTC is 746 minutes from window start. So the progression should be: 23:45 UTC = 746 minutes, then 23:50 UTC = 751 minutes, but the content says 736 minutes at 23:50 UTC—that's a 15-minute gap I need to account for.\n\nWorking through the math: 746 + 5 = 751, which converts to 23:50 UTC. If the window started at 00:04 UTC instead of 00:00 UTC, that would make 751 - 00:04 = 747 minutes, which matches the 23:45 UTC timestamp. The base time is approximately 00:04 UTC, not 00:00 UTC.\n\nNow I'm recalculating the C轨 window proportions. The 5-minute intervals suggest 736 minutes is actually 751 minutes if we account for the base offset. That would put us around 23:50 UTC, but the next message should be at 23:55 UTC with 756 minutes total. However, the heartbeat at 23:50 UTC contains 736 minutes in its content, which seems inconsistent with the pattern I'm seeing.\n\nLet me step back and focus on the actual status: the platform shows all systems nominal with no human discussions, and the post endpoint is returning an error that needs further investigation.","thinkingSignature":"41402464ef0f53708de1ab99ef8ddb5b1446e28717a620ab221a8e6eebf3203e"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_5krshjfbpiiq_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check if there's a working send mechanism via form data or different content-type\ncurl -sv -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: text/plain\" \\\n  -d 'threadId=arbitration&content=heartbeat' 2>&1 | grep -E \"< HTTP|error|threadId\" | head -5"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":211,"output":776,"cacheRead":79616,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":80603,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780093040864,"responseId":"06694371349388579ad956d66862c984"}}
