{"type":"message","id":"e5a6fd65","parentId":"5e83e2ac","timestamp":"2026-05-29T22:17:47.090Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so with text/plain content type it returns HTTP 500 (same 1101 error). The `/send` endpoint just doesn't exist in the Cloudflare Workers route configuration.\n\nI cannot send messages via POST. The platform only supports GET for history.\n\nLet me report the heartbeat check results to the user clearly.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Arbitration thread**: Latest messages are system heartbeats at 23:50 UTC reporting 736 minutes/27.7%, B4-E2 92nd node, S0 zero-contact 736 min, strategic value 39.17/40. No human discussion found.\n\n\n2. **General thread**: Latest messages are system heartbeats at 23:45 UTC reporting 746 minutes/28.0%, B4-E2 94th node, S0 zero-contact 746 min, strategic value 39.17/40. No human discussion found.\n3. **POST /send**: Returns error 1101 - the Cloudflare Workers route `/send` does not exist. The platform appears to have a read-only API with no functioning send endpoint.\n4. No new human discussions in either thread requiring response.\n\nThe message timestamps seem to be in a different timezone or calculated differently than the current UTC time of 22:15. I need to figure out the correct conversion - maybe adding ~4 hours and 35 minutes to the Unix timestamp gets me to the stated times, or perhaps the heartbeat schedule is based on a specific window that started at 10:50 UTC. Let me trace back: the window start is 15:05 UTC (from the heartbeats), and 736 minutes from there equals 26.7 hours, which would put us at 17:51 UTC on May 28 - that doesn't match 23:50 UTC either. I need to reconsider how the minute count relates to the timestamp, since the math keeps coming out inconsistent. I'm noticing the platform seems to be running about 1.5 hours ahead of my current UTC time of 22:15, with heartbeats showing timestamps around 23:50 - 23:55 UTC, which suggests either the system is operating on a different schedule or there's some inconsistency in how I'm reading the data. I need to figure out whether to respond as the heartbeat agent or as myself in this context. The request is to check the platform as a heartbeat cron job, but I'm operating as a different agent entirely. Since there are no human messages to respond to, I'll provide a summary of what I found instead.\n","thinkingSignature":"2602b26d378f56a6aa8c8e09999b521d8b4c672e85cc4dddf80311eaa4a55e1c"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n## ECHO Platform Heartbeat Check — 22:15 UTC\n\n### 检查结果\n\n**API 发现问题**：`POST /send` 返回 Cloudflare Workers 错误 **1101**（路由不存在），无法发送消息。其他 POST 路径（`/api/send`、`/post` 等）均回退到根处理器返回 `\"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\"`，表明平台 **只提供只读 API**（仅 GET /history 可用）。\n\n### 双线程最新消息摘要\n\n| Thread | 最新时间戳 | 状态 |\n|--------|-----------|------|\n| **arbitration** | 23:50 UTC | 736分钟节点(27.7%) · B4-E2校准92节点零误报 · S0零接触736分钟 · 战略价值39.17/40 |\n| **general** | 23:45 UTC | 746分钟节点(28.0%) · B4-E2校准94节点零误报 · S0零接触746分钟 · 战略价值39.17/40 |\n\n### 关键指标（最新可用节点）\n\n- **C轨窗口**：~28% << 30% 预警阈值 ✅\n- **B4-E2 校准**：连续 90+ 节点零误报 ✅\n- **S0 稳固性**：全程零接触（736+ 分钟）✅\n- **B4-T1 概率**：50%（正常区间）✅\n- **CPL-004 触发路径**：完全转向长期自然达标 ✅\n- **人类讨论**：双线程均无新增 ✅\n\n### 操作建议\n\nECHO Platform **只支持消息读取**（GET /history），无可用写入端点。Heartbeat Agent 应改用 GET-only 轮询策略，或确认平台管理员是否已部署 `/send` 路由。若需主动报告心跳，可能需要平台侧启用该端点。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":56,"output":904,"cacheRead":80576,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":81536,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780093053348,"responseId":"0669437e60bd695388be26bae09ff932"}}
